WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.510
The moment a baby is born, it is attacked
by several microbes present around.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.809
But not all organisms are successful in their
attack.

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:18.130
However, the body does not
always win the battle either!

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.700
There are many infections which successfully
infect

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.650
us, irrespective of our age groups.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.610
And not only this, but many a times it happens
that the same infection repeats its

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.610
occurrence!

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.220
Take the common cold for example!

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:37.800
It is one of the most common
infectious diseases caused by a virus known

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.140
as Rhinovirus.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.120
And what do we mean by infectious disease?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.850
The term “infectious” stands for
“liability of transmission”.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.210
And the term “disease” literally means
the body is

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.620
“NOT AT EASE”.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:57.120
So a Disease can be defined as an illness
caused by numerous factors, which

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.950
withholds the body from functioning normally.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.479
There is one more concept similar to this,
which we need to know.

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:07.430
It is called
“Disorder”.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:08.520
And what does that mean?

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.680
Well, the term literally means the body is
not able to work properly, or simply, is “out

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.860
of order”.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.060
So are the two conditions
different?

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.080
Well, technically yes!

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.460
Diseases are mainly caused by pathogens.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:29.450
That is, the external agents like viruses,
fungi, bacteria and so on, which enter the

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.620
body and create problems.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:36.590
On the other hand, disorders are caused by
some or the other defects in the

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.570
functioning of certain cells or tissues.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.420
Take diabetes for example.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.810
It can occur due
to either improper production or improper

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.890
uptake of insulin by the cells.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:56.270
Now, diseases are usually infectious or transmissible
whereas disorders are not!

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.200
There are many sources which use the term
“non-infectious diseases”

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.590
synonymously with “disorders”.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:06.369
But what are these “non-infectious diseases”
by

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:07.420
the way?

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.870
Non-infectious diseases, as the name suggests,
are those diseases which do not

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:14.379
spread with mere contact.

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:17.739
So logically they can be used interchangeably.

00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:22.659
But for now, we will not get into the details
of this classification of the types of

00:02:22.659 --> 00:02:23.659
Diseases.

00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:27.329
Rather, we will have a look at examples of
each type!

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:32.450
For studying infectious diseases in detail,
we will have a look at some known

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:37.620
diseases like Malaria, Typhoid and few others.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:43.189
On the other hand, for studying disorders,
or say the non-infectious ones, we will

00:02:43.189 --> 00:02:46.689
have a look at an important example like Cancer.

00:02:46.689 --> 00:02:51.929
Let us have a look at each one in detail in
the upcoming videos!

